                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "You don't need an `else` block here if you're jumping over the code using `goto cleanup;` on line 487.\n\nHowever, you can avoid the use of `goto` by inverting the `if` condition:\n\n```\nif ((rc == pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, rec_handle))) {\n    return rc;\n}\nif (record->is_remote == is_remote && rec_handle == record_handle) {\n    prev = pldm_pdr_get_prev_record(repo, record);\n    return pldm_pdr_remove_record(repo, record, prev);\n}\nrc = pldm_msgbuf_destroy(buf);\nif (rc) {\n    return rc;\n}\nrecord = record->next;\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/pdr.c",
                    "line": 490,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
